Falsifies `capability_manifest_note::verification::a_decoded_verb_table_finds_each_verb`.

The defect: `decode_verbs` stops checking that each verb sorts strictly after the one before. A
table out of order then decodes, and `grants_for`'s binary search misses a verb the table holds,
so a line naming that verb is granted nothing while the iterator lists its grants.

Expected to fail: the assertion that `grants_for` finds each decoded verb.

diff --git a/crates/capability_manifest_note/src/lib.rs b/crates/capability_manifest_note/src/lib.rs
index 2924ed822..330f4e33d 100644
--- a/crates/capability_manifest_note/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/capability_manifest_note/src/lib.rs
@@ -1421,9 +1421,6 @@ pub fn decode_verbs(d: &[u8]) -> Result<Verbs<'_>, Error> {
         {
             return Err(Error::BadField(at + grant_contract::MAXIMUM_VERB + 2));
         }
-        if previous.is_some_and(|p| !before(p, &word[..len])) {
-            return Err(Error::BadField(at));
-        }
         previous = Some(&word[..len]);
     }
     Ok(Verbs { records: &d[8..] })
